Do not assert on a stale non-H.264 avctx in has_decode_delay_been_guessed().

has_decode_delay_been_guessed() (libavformat/demux.c:788) asserts that the internal avctx is
H.264, or NONE and closed, once codecpar says H.264. A demuxer can switch codecpar to H.264
after the avctx was set up for another codec: the Ogg demuxer re-reads an OGM header for a
new chain link, sets need_context_update, and avformat_find_stream_info() reaches the EOF
branch (demux.c:3039) before another packet syncs the context. The avctx then still holds
the old codec, closed. Return early only for an opened decoder of another codec and let the
closed case fall through to the frame-count heuristic; nothing else reads the avctx there.
Commit 00b4d67812 relaxed the same assertion for the FLV case (NONE and closed).
Not fixed upstream as of 50276fac71 (2026-11-23).

Includes libavformat/tests/ogg_ogm_h264.c (fate-ogg-ogm-h264): two Ogg pages reduced from a
fuzzer input, a Vorbis BOS page and an OGM H.264 video header on a new serial, run through
avformat_find_stream_info(). Without the fix it fails the assertion.

Upstream: none found; related closed PR FFmpeg/FFmpeg#21215 (code.ffmpeg.org, 2025-12) proposed a soft check, 4bb9b46486 added the assertion instead.

